# 0006. blink.cmp for completion

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
Completion was nvim-cmp plus seven companion plugins (cmp-nvim-lsp, -buffer, -path, -cmdline,
cmp_luasnip, LuaSnip, lspkind); it was configured twice and lspkind icons never showed.

## Decision
Replace them with blink.cmp. Its native fuzzy matcher is fetched by `make sync`
(`scripts/blink-fuzzy.lua`).

## Alternatives
- Keep nvim-cmp and fix its config: eight plugins to keep in step.

## Rationale
One plugin instead of eight; typo-tolerant fuzzy matching; docs and signature help built in.

## Consequences
- LSP capabilities come from `blink.cmp` ([0004](0004-lsp-through-mason-and-native-vim-lsp.adr)).
- The fuzzy matcher is a binary that must be fetched per machine.

## References
- README "Design pass", `lua/plugins/coding.lua`
